  "source_contract": {
    "default": "Missing/undefined or actual null -> compatible. Empty/blank strings are invalid; no trimming or coercion.",
    "accepted": [
      "compatible",
      "native",
      "auto"
    ],
    "type_partition": "ConfigInput borrows Value or original JsDocument; nullish removes only missing/null. ConfigValue::text accepts actual string nodes only and ConfigText::is checks exact scalar/UTF16 units against ASCII literals. All other JSON node kinds, overflow numbers, singleton valid-string arrays, case variants and strings containing lone units cannot become accepted selector text.",
    "validation_order": "After global session/flags/evaluator and active/check-all Ollama model/timeout syntax/keepalive/auth-mode, before all tier model validation, Auto target eligibility, upstream and late numeric settings. The selector is global: neither evaluator masks an invalid profile.",
    "models": "Auto defaults Sonnet to claude-sonnet-5-5; other profiles use claude-sonnet-5; Haiku/Opus defaults unchanged. All tier names validate first. Auto then requires exact catalog-known Auto-capable Sonnet and Opus, in that order. Compatible/native keep valid custom aliases; no family-name inference.",
    "launch": "Only explicit final permission-mode auto before -- selects Auto. Configured profile otherwise survives; original args and permission settings are forwarded. Compatible forces child Haiku and MAX_THINKING_TOKENS=0; native preserves model/thinking; Auto fills only an absent OS-string model and preserves thinking/permission control variables. No account/admin eligibility claim.",
    "runtime": "Router uses ClientProfile::Auto OR independently recognized routable safeguards for Auto policy; Auto floors Haiku selection to Sonnet and applies exact target compatibility. TokenCounter carries config Auto into the same shared target policy. Actual original18 mock gateway tests establish human-turn switching, not real-provider eligibility/quality."
  },
